<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Which launcher art the AUTO icon wears, light half. The dark half is the values-night twin.

  🔴 Aliases, not a second copy of the art. Both variants are authored in Tate's icon pack and
  ported into `drawable/ic_launcher_{foreground,background}_{light,dark}.xml`, which are UNQUALIFIED
  on purpose: the app also offers "always light", "always dark" and OLED as an explicit choice
  (see the activity-aliases in AndroidManifest.xml), and a forced variant cannot be built out of a
  `-night` qualified drawable, because the qualifier resolves against the system's night mode and
  there is no way to ask for the other one. Naming the two variants outright and pointing the auto
  name at whichever the configuration wants gets both behaviours from one copy of the art.

  This is also why `drawable-night/` no longer exists here.
-->
<resources>
    <item name="ic_launcher_background" type="drawable">@drawable/ic_launcher_background_light</item>
    <item name="ic_launcher_foreground" type="drawable">@drawable/ic_launcher_foreground_light</item>
</resources>
